      "created_at" : "Fri Sep 20 02:42:17 +0000 2024",
      "favorited" : false,
      "full_text" : "@adspthepodcast At least you apologized.  In STL there are three algorithms used for rotate, Fletcher&amp;Silver for random access (n + gcd(n, k) assignments), 3-reverses for bidirectional iterators, and Griess&amp;Mills for Forward Iterators. Griess&amp;Mills is Euclid's subtractive GCD algorithm.",
      "lang" : "en",
      "in_reply_to_screen_name" : "adspthepodcast",
