      "full_text" : "@scottmichaud @ericniebler @DaveAbrahams @Cor3ntin I don't know their codebase. If they are getting use-after-free from passing raw-pointer obtained from unique pointers then shared_ptr might be the fix. I like the idea of banning unique_ptr::get - and may see if I can write (or get someone else to write) a clang-tidy rule.",
