      "full_text" : "@sdowney @Cor3ntin @MichaelCaisse @__phantomderp @tvaneerd It doesn't need an \"empty\" state - any more than an int needs an empty state. Consider this:\n\nint a[1'000];\niota(begin(a), end(a), 0);\n\nIt would be nice if I could write this as:\n\nint a[1'000]{iota(0)};\n\nBut I cannot. Nor can I initialize efficiently an array of spans.",
