      "full_text" : "@sdowney @Cor3ntin @MichaelCaisse @__phantomderp @tvaneerd The standard could (and probably should) remove the requirement of default construction entirely for regular. It was included initially for several reasons:\n1. To allow declaration of an object before initialization.\n2. To support move (before rvalue-refs)...\n2/n",
