      "created_at" : "Sat Mar 30 00:48:36 +0000 2024",
      "favorited" : false,
      "full_text" : "@ericniebler It isn't just that you block in main() but that you lose all parallelism. Structuring code to exploit parallelism with senders requires expressing more than one path of a fork with senders. The model of \"fork work, do work, join\" just serializes the work.",
      "lang" : "en",
