      "full_text" : "@DaveAbrahams @lorentey A relaxed memory policy on reading the use-count for a cow is safe but might end up making unnecessary copies. An increasing problem with larger and more levels of cache - so optimization? Maybe. Propose that `std::shared_ptr&lt;&gt;::use_count()` should take a memory policy?",
