      "full_text" : "@seanbax @contramork Say the compiler has the value 8 in register x and needs 64. It can be an order of magnitude faster to execute mul x x than load 64 from the data segment. Compilers should probably use constexpr as a strong hint to compile time evaluate... But C++ and C have As-If.",
