      "full_text" : "@tcanens @BarryRevzin @AlisdairMered @cjdb_ns @PeterSommerlad @lefticus And what is the state of a pointer, `p`, after `delete p;`? Answer to all, partially-formed. Partially-formed objects are unavoidable in the language. Trying to ignore them is only doing harm. `\"Valid but unspecified\" is not a requirement, it is nonsense.",
