      "full_text" : "@tcanens @BarryRevzin @AlisdairMered @cjdb_ns @PeterSommerlad @lefticus It would do much less damage, to require that a partially-formed state be a fixed-point. But I think the best answer is to let self-move fall into the category of modifying the same object twice without a sequence point, even if it _could_ be a `nop`.  Let a sanitizer catch it.",
