      "full_text" : "@tcanens @BarryRevzin @AlisdairMered @cjdb_ns @PeterSommerlad @lefticus The effective result is to require that most types have an `empty` valid state. i.e. almost everything becomes an `optional`. This is what happened with `variant`. Further, if this is allowed, a compiler cannot warn on modifying a value twice between sequence points 4/n",
