      "full_text" : "@tcanens @BarryRevzin @AlisdairMered @cjdb_ns @PeterSommerlad @lefticus Let's dissect self-swap - at the core the issue becomes:\n`a = move(a);`.  In _general_, a self-move is a potential contradiction. Consider a self-move of an arbitrary vector. The postcondition of being moved from is an empty vector. 1/n",
      "lang" : "en",
