      "full_text" : "@PeterSommerlad @lefticus @AlisdairMered Absolutely not true. There is not a single place in all the standard library where another operation is required for exception safety. Trying to satisfy well-formed is problematic, error-prone, and inefficient. See the long debates on the state of a variant post exception.",
