      "full_text" : "@AlisdairMered @PeterSommerlad @lefticus Consider a thread in a \"valid but unspecified\" state - you can't destruct it without risking termination. Two iterators cannot be equality compared without risking UB. And so on. That doesn't mean any type can't or shouldn't provide a stronger guarantee...",
