      "favorited" : false,
      "full_text" : "@TitusWinters A stable ABI means you can link against the platform API, shared library APIs including the standard, evolve your product without breaking plugins. C++ needs a strategy on how to specify and maintain ABI compatibility - not some \"one time break\" for efficiency. See @SwiftLang",
