      "created_at" : "Thu Jul 04 07:03:50 +0000 2019",
      "favorited" : false,
      "full_text" : "@TitusWinters @ciura_victor @isocpp Languages like ObjC recommend prefixing the name to avoid conflicts. In C++ this would be a namespace. So why not just require qualified names when using . notation. i.e. `v.stlab::gather(p);`. With a `using` a conflict would become an ambiguity same as a standalone function.",
