      "favorited" : false,
      "full_text" : "@sdowney @tvaneerd @lefticus @cjdb_ns One form or the other may be more efficient (in space, energy, and/or memory). We can reason about in-situ operations, cache locality, memory usage, etc., while maintaining functional \"purity\". The problem isn't object identity, but fragile relationships using identities. [2/2]",
