      "full_text" : "@tvaneerd @JamesWidman @lefticus @cjdb_ns Generic programming is VOP with a high emphasis on the importance of Regular Types. GP is not just compile-time. VOP is distinguished by shunning the notion that most everything is indirectly referenced, mutable, and shared. Mutability is limited to an implementation detail.",
