      "full_text" : "@adspthepodcast @ninkibah Many early Mac OS apps were written in Object Pascal, including Photoshop https://t.co/SMtn9ZQTJo It was the rise of Unix in enterprise and research that caused C to displace Pascal at the system level and created the opportunity for C++ to replace Object Pascal. 2/n",
