      "full_text" : "@adspthepodcast @ninkibah Listening to the talk of Pascal - so much that isn't mentioned. The Apple Lisa and Mac OS were written in a combination of Pascal and 68K assembly. Apple worked with Wirth to create Clascal (Pascal with Classes) for the Lisa Toolkit apps. This evolved into Object Pascal. 1/n",
